Below is a self-contained Python function that (1) repeats/concatenates a list the requested number of times, (2) flattens one level if some elements are sequences, and (3) returns the mode of the flattened list. The function first tries to use a (hypothetical) newer statistics library (named "statx" here, representing a 2025+ library if installed). If that library is not available it falls back to a pure-Python implementation that returns a ModeResult with numpy arrays, matching the example output format and tie-breaking by choosing the smallest value when multiple items tie for highest count.

